cyberpunk developer has opened up about  more changes coming to the game and  elden ring fans have discovered a  missing feature  let's start with cyberpunk reddit user  camille cesaro posted a twitter clip  from cyberpunk 2077 quest director paul  sasco in which the developer provided a  brief behind-the-scenes view of cd  projekt red's priorities sasko said  quote i can assure you that we are  working on an expansion we're working on  stuff you guys besides that that didn't  change we are still improving the game  because we are all aware there is work  to be done this is in line with cd  projekt red's message from a year ago  about how abandoning cyberpunk 2077  isn't an option sasko continued by  saying that's as much as i can tell you  we're working on stuff for you like i'm  literally daily reviewing quests or  talking to people about stuff so it's  happening patch 1.5 made sweeping  quality of life adjustments to cyberpunk  2077 such as options to skip its  needlessly long braindance tutorial or  respect your skills the patch also added  ps5 and xbox series x and s versions of  the game as well as the ability to buy  and customize apartments and receive  saucy photos from your romance options  but that's enough talking about games  that gain features let's talk about how  elden ring lost a feature before most of  us even got our hands on it youtuber  shakiro dubai and lance mcdonald managed  to find one of the most exciting  discoveries from eldon ring's network  test build this involves an npc  character that was cut from the final  release named monk jinko this npc would  have occupied the scavenger shack near  the approach to stormville castle and  would offer to brew the player an  alcoholic beverage once forbidden to  mortals called dream brew he only asked  that the player bring him the  ingredients in order to do this the npc  gives the player a new unique item saint  trina's crystal ball which is used to  collect slumber fog from sleeping  enemies and features its own unique  harvesting animation enemies that can  have their dreams harvested can't be  woken up unless attacked and have a  small cloud of fog surrounding their  head sakiro speculates that given the  monk's location at the scavenger shack  and how collecting dream fog works the  mechanic could have been an early method  for acquiring spirit summons or it could  have been for some entirely different  questline or purpose and fun fact about  me my favorite movie is inception so i  would love to steal people's dreams in  eldon ring and i know  leo wasn't stealing dreams in the movie  but so what i'm just connecting to  things i love don't steal my dream of  this getting patched back in i want to  use it now let's talk about another cool  discovery you can attach an external  graphics card to a steam deck it's not  easy but youtuber eta prime proved that  it's most definitely possible in a 10  minute video prime walks viewers through  the steps of opening the steam deck  replacing the ssd with the gpu that's  connected via an adapter held in place  with tape and attached to an external  power supply this is definitely not the  setup you're going to want on your  commute to work or to entertain yourself  on a long flight however with this gpu  attached prime was able to get witcher 3  to run at 4k at around 108 fps on ultra  settings unfortunately though the  results aren't all as impressive as that  example and prime explained that more  recently released titles will be  bottlenecked no matter what gpu is  attached whoa whoa whoa was something  like this possible for the switch has  someone done it already i mean i guess  it wouldn't matter you can't change  graphical settings on a switch so even  with a beefier gpu mario kart 8 is still  going to look like mario kart 8.  oh well let me know in the comments when  you think the switch pro is finally  going to come out and whoever gets the  closest answer to the actual release  date has to buy me one when it drops all  right i'll see you tomorrow  you
 

